    {
      "text": "Aerodactyl is a Pokémon from the age of dinosaurs. It was regenerated from genetic material extracted from amber. It is imagined to have been the king of the skies in ancient times.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Pokémon from the age of the dinosaurs. It used its sawlike fangs to shred its prey before eating them.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "In ancient times, it ruled the skies. A widely accepted theory is that it went extinct due to a large meteor impact.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Restored from DNA found in amber, this Pokémon exhibited ferocity that was greater than expected. Some casualties resulted.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It flew through the open skies over the ancient continent as if they were its own. When it touched ground, its walk was weak and slow.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "A savage Pokémon that died out in ancient times. It was resurrected using DNA taken from amber.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "A savage Pokémon that died out in ancient times. It was resurrected using DNA taken from amber.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a ferocious Pokémon from ancient times. Apparently even modern technology is incapable of producing a perfectly restored specimen.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aerodactyl’s sawlike fangs can shred skin to tatters—even the skin of Steel-type Pokémon.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
